## 8. Design rationale and assumptions
* Update interval for UDP stream: 2 s. Max file size 10 MB. Filenames limited to `[A-Za-z0-9._-]` so a client cannot escape the storage directory.
* SYSINFO values read from /proc (loadavg 1-min as `cpu_load`, MemTotal−MemAvailable as `mem_used_mb`, /proc/uptime).
* Responses must be one line, so EXEC output has newlines replaced by spaces.
* After 3 failed AUTH attempts the Agent closes the connection (assumption — not in the brief).
* Oversized uploads are drained (up to 64 MB) so the TCP stream stays framed correctly; larger claims close the connection.
* Uploads are written to a temp file and renamed so GET never serves a half-written file.
* Concurrent uploads of the same filename: last rename wins (documented limitation).
* Optional extension implemented: throughput (bytes/s) for PUT and GET in the Controller.
